  "answer": "Yes, this is a real bug. When requests are preempted due to KV cache pressure, their ProgressIndex is reset to 0 (sim/batch_formation.go:232), causing them to re-execute the full prefill+decode sequence. Each decode step increments sim.Metrics.TotalOutputTokens++ (sim/simulator.go:647), so preempted requests have their output tokens counted multiple times. The fix subtracts the already-counted output tokens when a request is preempted and resets the per-request ITL slice to avoid inflated inter-token latency metrics. With the fix, both runs report total_output_tokens=105082 (previously 114630 with small KV vs 105082 with large KV).",
